Describe $P$ by how far you go from $B$ along $BC$ (distance $u$) and then parallel to $BA$ (distance $v$). With side $s$:

- moving from $P$ parallel to $CB$ (to the left), you reach $AB$ after $u$: so $u = 2$;
- moving from $P$ parallel to $AC$ (down to the right), you reach $BC$ after $v$: so $v = 6$;
- moving from $P$ parallel to $BA$ (up to the right), you reach $AC$ after $s - u - v$: so $s - 8 = 3$.

Hence $s = 11$ and the perimeter is $33$ m.

**Answer: (C) 33 m**
